            },
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "ffffd208-eb09-4da3-b516-f8bc695758dd",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=ffffd208-eb09-4da3-b516-f8bc695758dd",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### The definition\n\nTo compare pyramids, we first need to define what a pyramid is.\n\nFor this, we will use Eric W. Weisstein's definition: pyramids *are a geometric figure with a closed base and whose lateral faces are triangles that meet at a common point at the top, called the apex*",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<img src=\"http://www.historytracers.org/images/HistoryTracers/pentagonal_pyramid.jpg\" id=\"img0\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('img0', '0%')\"  class=\"imgcenter\"/>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": [],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "*Pentagonal Base Pyramid following the mathematical definition*",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "ee2d3587-30a6-4a45-9032-555441b3b829",
         "prev": "",
